      "writtenOn": "2023-08-03T17:50:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The fact that we don\u0027t even know what the command looks like is not a good signal of us doing the right thing.\n\nWe probably ask for documentation around what it looks like, in order to know what the parsing should do.\nalso if this is passed as argument `,,` the initial version was taking it as a `0`.\n\nBtw, in you previous comment, we forgot to take into consideration that `strchr` can return null when there is no match, and then `p_s++` will no longer be null",
